WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.851
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.950 --> 00:08.436
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.471 --> 00:12.123
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.141 --> 00:15.125
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.160 --> 00:18.630
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.663 --> 00:21.949
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.983 --> 00:23.517
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.568 --> 00:25.185
♪ Laugh and cry

00:25.236 --> 00:27.236
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.412 --> 00:41.363
There he is. The reason
my bedpost is so shiny.

00:41.612 --> 00:44.138
Oh my God. Are you still
obsessed with Kent?

00:44.242 --> 00:45.569
Just ask him out already.

00:45.669 --> 00:47.325
The worse that can
happen is he says no.

00:47.403 --> 00:49.577
Are you kidding?
Of course he'll say no.

00:49.653 --> 00:51.614
There's no way he'd
ever go out with me.

00:51.672 --> 00:54.538
He's just so...
dreamy.

00:55.878 --> 00:58.121
Oh Kent, what are we gonna do?

00:58.153 --> 01:00.861
With the Earth destroyed,
we're the only two humans left.

01:01.114 --> 01:03.648
Well then, it looks like
we need to start repopulating.

01:10.532 --> 01:13.951
♪ Meg and Kent
are having space sex ♪

01:13.985 --> 01:15.586
♪ We can't show it

01:15.620 --> 01:18.405
♪ But that's what's happening.

01:18.456 --> 01:22.243
(Meg moaning)

01:22.294 --> 01:23.427
(gagging)

01:23.461 --> 01:24.628
I think she's choking.

01:24.663 --> 01:25.863
Should we wake her up?

01:25.897 --> 01:28.231
No, she's got to learn
to breathe out of her nose.

01:28.266 --> 01:29.633
(breathing heavily)

01:29.668 --> 01:31.701
She's getting it.

01:35.307 --> 01:37.106
Peter, you want
another waffle?

01:37.141 --> 01:38.208
I can't Lois.

01:38.242 --> 01:39.976
I promised Janice
I'd take her shift.

01:40.010 --> 01:41.845
Can I get two eggs,
scrambled, on toast?

01:41.879 --> 01:43.947
Sure thing, honey. Adam and
Eve on a raft, wreck them!

01:43.981 --> 01:46.583
I'd like a hotdog with ketchup
and some Jell-O, please.

01:46.617 --> 01:48.968
Paint a bow-wow red and a
side of nervous pudding!

01:49.003 --> 01:50.970
Can I have a well-done burger
with lettuce and tomato?

01:51.005 --> 01:53.339
Burn one, drag it through
the garden, pin a rose on it!

01:53.374 --> 01:54.574
Can I use your bathroom?

01:54.608 --> 01:56.141
Got a telephone pole heading
to the swimming hole.

01:56.175 --> 01:57.376
Spray it with sunshine!

01:58.979 --> 02:00.412
Psst.

02:00.446 --> 02:02.264
Hey, dog.
What?

02:02.298 --> 02:03.999
You want in?

02:04.033 --> 02:06.618
Yeah.

02:06.669 --> 02:07.953
Ah, look at this.

02:08.004 --> 02:10.939
She's taped photographs of
Virginia Woolf and Katy Perry

02:10.974 --> 02:13.375
on the inside cover,
as if she's some sort

02:13.409 --> 02:14.977
of hip hybrid
of those two things.

02:15.011 --> 02:16.445
Ugh. Yeah, like
she could ever write

02:16.479 --> 02:17.746
<i>Who's Afraid of
Virginia Woolf?</i>

02:17.780 --> 02:19.448
<i>Brian,
Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf?</i>

02:19.482 --> 02:21.450
was not written
by Virginia Woolf.

02:21.484 --> 02:22.784
Yeah, obviously.

02:22.819 --> 02:24.752
But, you know, it's-it's
pretty much about her.

02:24.786 --> 02:26.555
It really isn't, Brian.

02:26.589 --> 02:29.574
Let's, uh, let's just
get into this, huh?

02:30.876 --> 02:33.510
"Dear Diary, got
down to 152 today.

02:33.545 --> 02:35.046
Think that's a
nice weight for me."

02:35.080 --> 02:36.364
Oh, here's another one.

02:36.398 --> 02:39.400
"Dear Diary, just discovered
the music of John Denver.

02:39.434 --> 02:42.003
Wow-wee, where's this been?"

02:42.037 --> 02:43.421
Hey, look at this.

02:43.454 --> 02:45.790
"Kent is so incredibly sexy.

02:45.824 --> 02:48.292
"He said 'hi' to me
today, and I almost died.

02:48.327 --> 02:52.696
"Also, I learned a funny lesson
today in my pursuit of Kent:

02:52.731 --> 02:55.999
anal bleaching is better
left to professionals. LOL."

02:56.033 --> 02:58.635
Oh, oh!
No, no, no, come on, now, come on.

02:58.669 --> 03:01.620
Jeez, it's just pages and pages
of stuff about this Kent guy.

03:01.638 --> 03:02.938
She's really obsessed with him.

03:02.974 --> 03:04.690
Well, obsession's not such
a bad thing.

03:04.724 --> 03:06.692
It got us
the first printing press.

03:06.726 --> 03:08.094
You're a whore, Sheila,

03:08.129 --> 03:10.130
and I'm gonna make sure
everybody knows it!

03:21.858 --> 03:23.308
Here!

03:23.326 --> 03:25.260
I can't read.

03:25.294 --> 03:26.729
No one can read.

03:31.717 --> 03:33.335
Bye, Patty. Bye, Esther.

03:33.370 --> 03:34.786
Bye, overzealous Asian kids

03:34.820 --> 03:37.072
lining up to be the first ones
in school tomorrow.

03:37.107 --> 03:39.374
Go away. No time
to say "bye."

03:39.425 --> 03:42.560
(laughs) I pass you
'cause you lose focus!

03:42.594 --> 03:44.212
Damn! Lost focus!

03:44.246 --> 03:46.247
Life over!

03:55.339 --> 03:59.009
Oh, Kent,
this is all I ever wanted.

03:59.027 --> 04:00.477
I feel the same way, Meg.

04:00.511 --> 04:03.981
From today onward,
this is our life.

04:04.015 --> 04:05.682
We should get
off the horse soon.

04:05.701 --> 04:08.286
I want to save one for you.

04:08.320 --> 04:10.320
(horn honking, tires squealing)

04:11.973 --> 04:13.106
Oh, my God!

04:13.141 --> 04:14.458
Are you all right?

04:14.492 --> 04:15.542
I'm fine.

04:15.576 --> 04:17.678
Lucky for you,
this tree was my destination.

04:20.414 --> 04:23.250
And the job exchange begins.

04:23.284 --> 04:25.018
Sir, do you want to move ahead

04:25.053 --> 04:27.753
on the agreement
with the sanitation union?

04:27.788 --> 04:29.789
Sir, we need leadership.

04:29.823 --> 04:30.973
Oh, my God, Meg!

04:31.008 --> 04:32.208
Are you okay?

04:32.242 --> 04:33.359
Yeah, I-I'm fine.

04:33.393 --> 04:35.628
I guess I got distracted again
thinking about Kent.

04:35.662 --> 04:37.580
Oh, I can't do this anymore.

04:37.614 --> 04:39.849
I've just got to ask him out.

04:39.883 --> 04:41.433
Sorry!

04:47.574 --> 04:49.308
Honey, give me
any laundry you have.

04:49.342 --> 04:51.243
I'm doing a diapers
and Meg load.

04:51.278 --> 04:53.311
Hey, Mom, can I ask you
about something?

04:53.345 --> 04:55.480
Of course, Meg.
What's on your mind?

04:55.514 --> 04:57.415
Well, there's this guy
I like at school,

04:57.450 --> 04:59.084
and I was thinking about,

04:59.118 --> 05:02.237
I-I don't know, maybe
calling him and...

05:02.271 --> 05:04.906
Meg, are you asking,
in this day and age,

05:04.940 --> 05:07.342
when the CEO of Xerox
is a woman,

05:07.376 --> 05:09.643
when the president
of Brazil is a woman,

05:09.677 --> 05:11.578
even Rosie O'Donnell
is a woman,

05:11.613 --> 05:13.581
whether it's appropriate
for a girl

05:13.616 --> 05:15.517
to ask a boy out on a date?

05:15.551 --> 05:17.519
Of course it's appropriate.

05:17.553 --> 05:21.088
It's also sad and desperate
and I would never do it,

05:21.122 --> 05:22.990
but you're not me,
are you, sweetie?

05:23.024 --> 05:24.224
No, I'm not.

05:24.259 --> 05:26.260
(laughing):
No, you're not.

05:28.596 --> 05:31.165
(sighs)

05:31.199 --> 05:32.866
(phone rings)

05:32.901 --> 05:34.467
Hello?
Hey, Kent?

05:34.501 --> 05:36.170
It's Meg, from
English class.

05:36.204 --> 05:37.538
Uh...

05:37.572 --> 05:38.772
And math class?

05:38.807 --> 05:40.173
And bio?

05:40.207 --> 05:42.341
And the Facebook campaign
to get me to kill myself?

05:42.377 --> 05:43.476
Oh, Meg!

05:43.510 --> 05:45.144
Hey, what's up?
Hey!

05:45.179 --> 05:46.612
Um, nothing much.

05:46.647 --> 05:48.782
I was just wondering

05:48.816 --> 05:51.117
if you maybe wanted
to hang out some time?

05:51.151 --> 05:52.318
Sure.

05:52.352 --> 05:54.587
Oh, wow, cool!

05:54.621 --> 05:57.290
Okay, um,
I'll-I'll text you?

05:57.324 --> 05:58.508
(beeps)

05:58.542 --> 06:01.177
(screams)
Yes! I can't believe it!

06:01.211 --> 06:04.713
Oh, my God, I'm going out
on a date with Kent Lastname.

06:04.747 --> 06:06.364
Yes! Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

06:06.399 --> 06:07.466
(screams)

06:07.484 --> 06:08.718
Oh, my gosh!

06:08.752 --> 06:11.653
I'm gonna go ahead
and shut this for you.

06:17.642 --> 06:19.409
(knocking)

06:21.012 --> 06:22.062
Oh, hello.

06:22.097 --> 06:23.497
Hi, you must be
Mrs. Griffin.

06:23.531 --> 06:25.449
I'm Kent.
I'm here to pick up Meg.

06:25.483 --> 06:27.384
Oh, Kent, it's so
nice to meet you.

06:27.419 --> 06:28.851
She's just getting ready.

06:28.886 --> 06:30.587
Meg, Kent's here!

06:30.622 --> 06:32.522
Just putting on my lipstick.

06:32.556 --> 06:33.956
Damn it.

06:33.991 --> 06:35.958
And this is Meg's brother,
Chris.

06:35.993 --> 06:37.493
Oh, yeah,
I've seen you around school.

06:37.528 --> 06:38.961
You eat
with the deaf kids, right?

06:38.996 --> 06:41.030
One of them isn't
all the way deaf.

06:41.065 --> 06:42.665
What grade are you in again?

06:42.700 --> 06:45.000
That's still being worked
out by a team of counselors.

06:45.034 --> 06:46.935
Cool.
Hope to see you around school.

06:46.969 --> 06:48.604
He seems nice.

06:48.639 --> 06:49.756
Sorry, I missed all that.

06:49.807 --> 06:50.873
I was tweeting.

06:59.582 --> 07:02.584
<i>MOVIE ANNOUNCER: Coming this fall,
the prequel to Philadelphia.</i>

07:02.618 --> 07:04.286
Are you sure
we don't need a condom?

07:04.321 --> 07:05.821
No, it's okay,
I'm a lawyer.

07:05.855 --> 07:08.974
(loud kissing noises)

07:09.008 --> 07:11.308
(yawns)

07:11.344 --> 07:14.112
How you girls doing on popcorn?

07:14.163 --> 07:15.480
I'll take some.

07:15.515 --> 07:16.947
Here you go.

07:16.982 --> 07:19.751
(yawns)

07:19.786 --> 07:22.803
Oh, sorry, am I taking
up the whole armrest?

07:24.106 --> 07:26.624
Boy, it's kind
of chilly in here.

07:26.658 --> 07:29.193
Really? You got big sweat
marks under your boobs.

07:29.227 --> 07:32.063
That must mean
they must like you then.

07:32.097 --> 07:33.414
(forced giggling)

07:33.448 --> 07:34.749
Hey, I'll be
right back.

07:34.783 --> 07:36.833
I got to go to
the bathroom.

07:36.867 --> 07:38.886
Oh, thank God.

07:43.107 --> 07:44.491
And now,
our feature presentation:

07:44.525 --> 07:48.027
<i>Adrien Brody Doing Sit-Ups
in 3-D.</i>

07:49.663 --> 07:50.663
ADRIEN BRODY:
One.

07:50.698 --> 07:51.764
(crowd screams)

07:51.782 --> 07:53.767
Two.
(screams)

07:53.801 --> 07:56.469
(tires squeak)

07:56.504 --> 07:58.637
That was fun.

07:58.671 --> 08:00.173
We should hang out
again some time.

08:00.207 --> 08:01.408
Yeah, definitely.

08:01.442 --> 08:02.942
Well, good night.

08:02.977 --> 08:04.210
Night.

08:04.244 --> 08:06.679
Oh, no, I'm sorry.
Oh, my God, I thought you...

08:06.714 --> 08:09.548
I didn't think this was a date.
Oh, my God. I'm so embarrassed!

08:09.583 --> 08:11.551
Hey, it's 10:30!

08:11.585 --> 08:14.636
I suggest you take your dope
and go elsewhere!

08:14.671 --> 08:16.338
I'm sorry, Meg. I
think you're great,

08:16.372 --> 08:17.873
and I love hanging
out with you,

08:17.908 --> 08:19.975
but there's something
you should know.

08:20.009 --> 08:21.543
I'm gay.

08:21.578 --> 08:22.977
You are?

08:23.011 --> 08:26.081
Look, I really like you as a
friend, but to be honest...

08:26.115 --> 08:27.850
I like Chris.

08:27.884 --> 08:29.051
What?

08:29.085 --> 08:30.202
Oh, for God's sake.

08:30.236 --> 08:31.903
I have a shoe appointment
in the morning,

08:31.937 --> 08:33.322
and I want to be fresh!

08:33.356 --> 08:35.424
Yeah, the person
I'm attracted to

08:35.457 --> 08:36.724
is your brother.

08:36.758 --> 08:38.626
Brother?

08:38.660 --> 08:40.077
Rupert, did you hear that?

08:40.112 --> 08:42.079
Meg's boyfriend
is in love with me.

08:42.114 --> 08:43.414
Not that I care.

08:43.449 --> 08:45.500
I mean, it won't matter
once I explain to him

08:45.534 --> 08:47.268
what's going on with us.

08:47.302 --> 08:51.138
But what would I tell him
is going on with us?

08:54.510 --> 08:56.527
(sobbing)

09:08.139 --> 09:10.140
(sobbing continues)

09:20.567 --> 09:22.351
Thanks, Brian!

09:22.369 --> 09:23.786
Brian?

09:23.820 --> 09:26.021
Hey... princess.

09:26.056 --> 09:27.757
I'll get out of your hair.

09:27.792 --> 09:29.358
I can see you want
to be left alone.

09:29.376 --> 09:31.760
Why does everything bad
always happen to me?

09:31.795 --> 09:33.128
Huh, you and me both.

09:33.163 --> 09:35.014
I got this cold.
(coughing)

09:35.048 --> 09:37.650
And it's-it's
just in that

09:37.684 --> 09:40.152
"I don't want to give it to
a friend" stage, you know?

09:40.187 --> 09:41.787
(sniffling)
Oh, God, you hear that?

09:41.821 --> 09:43.722
I sound like a
Jewish See 'n Say.

09:43.757 --> 09:46.057
The uncle says...

09:46.091 --> 09:48.760
(phlegmy coughing)

09:48.812 --> 09:50.395
The grandpa says...

09:50.429 --> 09:52.181
GRANDPA:
What?!

09:52.214 --> 09:53.231
The aunt says...

09:53.265 --> 09:54.916
AUNT:
Oh-h.

09:54.950 --> 09:56.584
Kent told me he's gay,

09:56.619 --> 09:58.920
and even worse,
he likes Chris!

09:58.954 --> 10:01.089
Oh, wow, I'm really
sorry to hear that, Meg.

10:01.123 --> 10:02.423
I don't get it.

10:02.458 --> 10:04.692
I've been going to high school
with him for three years,

10:04.726 --> 10:06.861
and I always assumed
he was straight.

10:06.896 --> 10:08.696
Well, high school's
a tough time, Meg.

10:08.731 --> 10:10.031
Maybe he thought
he was straight,

10:10.065 --> 10:11.698
but then realized
he's gay.

10:11.733 --> 10:13.251
He's probably still
figuring things out.

10:13.285 --> 10:15.035
Hang in there.

10:15.070 --> 10:17.304
Well, I'll help him
figure things out.

10:17.338 --> 10:20.324
I'll help him figure out
that he's straight.

10:24.178 --> 10:26.179
That was really close.

10:31.018 --> 10:32.785
Hey, Chris, you
mind if I sit here?

10:32.819 --> 10:33.921
No, of course not.

10:33.955 --> 10:36.823
We were just having
a political discussion.

10:46.116 --> 10:48.701
Bill's, uh...
kind of conservative.

10:48.735 --> 10:50.202
Hey, you know,
it was really cool

10:50.237 --> 10:51.503
meeting you the
other night.

10:51.538 --> 10:53.356
I was thinking maybe we
should hang out sometime.

10:53.389 --> 10:56.392
Sure. I sleep for, like, six
hours every day after school,

10:56.426 --> 10:58.344
but other than that,
I'm pretty open.

10:58.377 --> 10:59.612
Well, great, then
we should definitely...

10:59.645 --> 11:01.046
Oh, hey, Meg.

11:01.080 --> 11:03.632
Listen, I hope you're okay
after the other night.

11:03.666 --> 11:04.899
Yeah, no,
that's-that's what

11:04.934 --> 11:06.534
I wanted to talk to
you about, Kent.

11:06.569 --> 11:09.137
Look, I-I know you're going
through a confusing time.

11:09.171 --> 11:10.705
The thing is, though,

11:10.741 --> 11:13.441
I feel like you're
not actually gay.

11:13.476 --> 11:14.726
What?

11:14.760 --> 11:16.428
No, I-I told you, I am.

11:16.462 --> 11:17.979
You don't talk
or act gay.

11:18.014 --> 11:19.481
I mean, you
play football.

11:19.515 --> 11:21.316
Those jeans cost
20 bucks, tops.

11:21.350 --> 11:23.517
And you only use
"hello" as a greeting,

11:23.552 --> 11:25.520
not as a way to outdo
some imaginary antagonist

11:25.554 --> 11:26.788
in conversation.

11:26.822 --> 11:27.988
Meg, please stop.

11:28.024 --> 11:29.757
I know your heart's
in the right place, but...

11:29.791 --> 11:30.858
Actually, it's not.

11:30.892 --> 11:32.693
It's a serious
medical condition.

11:32.727 --> 11:36.180
Yeah, that's...
that's not supposed to be there,

11:36.214 --> 11:39.149
so she should probably
always wear a hat.

11:42.253 --> 11:43.704
Hey.
Hey.

11:43.755 --> 11:45.756
So I guess you heard
about Meg's boyfriend, huh?

11:45.790 --> 11:47.224
I did.
I did hear, yes.

11:47.258 --> 11:48.358
Weird, right?

11:48.392 --> 11:50.010
Guy has a crush
on her own brother.

11:50.045 --> 11:51.228
I know, so weird.

11:51.262 --> 11:53.496
But, you know, the heart wants
what the heart wants.

11:53.530 --> 11:54.965
I just hope it doesn't
cause awkwardness,

11:55.000 --> 11:56.065
you know, in the house.

11:56.100 --> 11:57.635
Oh, no, it doesn't have
to be awkward,

11:57.668 --> 11:58.985
not if we don't make it awkward.

11:59.019 --> 12:00.486
I just don't see
the attraction.

12:00.521 --> 12:02.388
I mean, is it all
about that big package?

12:02.423 --> 12:03.990
Big? You really think so?

12:04.024 --> 12:05.992
Are you kidding?
Biggest in the family.

12:06.026 --> 12:08.293
That thing should be hanging
from the ceiling of a deli.

12:08.328 --> 12:09.495
Thanks, Brian.

12:09.529 --> 12:11.230
God, I have
so much energy now.

12:11.265 --> 12:15.001
(giggling): Am I the only one
who feels like grabbing a drink?

12:19.373 --> 12:21.858
Hey, do you think
this picture is hot?

12:23.761 --> 12:25.061
Kind of, yeah.

12:25.095 --> 12:27.295
<i>Well guess what:
that's my back.</i>

12:27.330 --> 12:28.831
Hook up with me!
Come on!

12:28.865 --> 12:30.165
We can make this work.

12:30.199 --> 12:32.434
Just stick your head in here
and pretend it's a butt.

12:32.468 --> 12:33.719
No, Meg, stop it.

12:33.753 --> 12:35.253
God, this is
getting too weird.

12:35.288 --> 12:37.489
I can't be
your boyfriend.

12:37.523 --> 12:41.093
In fact, I don't even
think I can be your friend.

12:41.127 --> 12:42.159
Kent, wait!

12:42.194 --> 12:43.612
We can totally be friends.

12:43.646 --> 12:45.080
We can go shopping together.

12:45.113 --> 12:47.164
And I like musicals.
I've even seen

12:47.199 --> 12:49.533
the latest Tony Award-winning
piece of crap.

12:49.568 --> 12:51.419
♪ If more people join in

12:51.453 --> 12:53.654
♪ The song will get better

12:53.689 --> 12:55.206
♪ If more people join in

12:55.240 --> 12:57.274
♪ The song will get better

12:57.309 --> 12:59.110
♪ If more people join in

12:59.161 --> 13:00.978
♪ The song will get better

13:01.012 --> 13:03.196
♪ If more people join in

13:03.230 --> 13:05.115
♪ The song will get better

13:05.149 --> 13:06.867
♪ Now you're having fun

13:06.901 --> 13:08.901
♪ 'Cause we're in the aisles

13:08.919 --> 13:12.423
♪ Even the bad guy
is singing along. ♪

13:12.457 --> 13:16.176
They're singing right near me,
so it's a great musical.

13:20.264 --> 13:21.848
Hey, Meg, what's wrong?

13:21.882 --> 13:24.017
What's wrong
is that Kent doesn't like me.

13:24.051 --> 13:25.684
He likes my brother, Chris.

13:25.719 --> 13:26.720
Oh, my God.

13:26.754 --> 13:27.821
No way!

13:27.855 --> 13:29.089
Well, I mean,

13:29.123 --> 13:30.440
you've done
everything you can do.

13:30.474 --> 13:32.107
I guess you just
have to move on.

13:32.142 --> 13:35.177
Yeah, I mean, there's a lot of
sweet guy-trim at this school.

13:35.211 --> 13:36.645
You-you don't understand.

13:36.680 --> 13:37.981
He's all I think about.

13:38.015 --> 13:39.782
I-I can't eat, I can't sleep.

13:39.816 --> 13:42.918
Just thinking about him now
gives me heart palpitations.

13:42.952 --> 13:44.520
(heart thumping)

13:44.554 --> 13:47.923
I feel like if I could just know
what it's like to be with him,

13:47.957 --> 13:49.658
just-just once,

13:49.692 --> 13:51.627
I could at least have
some sort of closure.

13:51.661 --> 13:53.429
Well, if Kent hooks up
with your brother,

13:53.463 --> 13:54.562
you could just have Chris

13:54.597 --> 13:56.231
describe every last detail
to you.

13:56.265 --> 13:58.382
Oh, my God, that's it.

13:58.417 --> 13:59.517
What do you mean?

13:59.551 --> 14:01.203
I mean,
if I can't have Kent,

14:01.236 --> 14:02.904
then that's
the next best thing.

14:02.939 --> 14:05.306
I've just got to get Chris
to sleep with him.

14:05.340 --> 14:06.674
Oh, no.

14:06.708 --> 14:07.975
Here comes
Mr. Davis with one

14:08.010 --> 14:10.645
of his technically-not-
illegal invitations.

14:10.679 --> 14:13.581
Girls, I'm gonna be
at the park later.

14:19.745 --> 14:21.978
Oh, I wouldn't worry
about it, Bonnie.

14:22.013 --> 14:24.048
I've put Stewie in the oven
a bunch of times.

14:24.082 --> 14:25.749
As long as you come
to your senses

14:25.783 --> 14:28.084
within 15 minutes,
everything's fine.

14:28.119 --> 14:30.137
Lois, can I go Slip 'N
Slide in the yard?

14:30.171 --> 14:32.005
Has it been half an hour
since you've eaten?

14:32.039 --> 14:33.373
Yes. Almost.

14:33.407 --> 14:35.759
Okay, I just want to be sure
you don't get a cramp.

14:35.793 --> 14:38.328
Yay! Poor people
water fun!

14:39.730 --> 14:41.297
Hey, Chris.

14:41.332 --> 14:43.400
Uh, can I ask you a question?

14:43.434 --> 14:44.668
Sure, what's up?

14:44.702 --> 14:47.370
Um, remember that "free hug"
coupon you gave me

14:47.405 --> 14:49.305
for my ninth birthday
that I never used?

14:49.339 --> 14:50.507
Yeah.

14:50.540 --> 14:52.691
Well, I'd like to use it.

14:52.726 --> 14:54.845
Oh, okay. Sure.

14:54.879 --> 14:58.180
But... I'd like
to sort of upgrade it.

14:58.215 --> 15:01.183
I'd like it
to be a butt-hug with Kent.

15:01.218 --> 15:03.051
What? Are you out
of your mind?!

15:03.086 --> 15:04.720
Chris, please,
just sleep with Kent

15:04.754 --> 15:06.187
and then tell me
all about it.

15:06.222 --> 15:07.388
Forget it, Meg.

15:07.423 --> 15:09.457
I can't just do stuff
with another guy.

15:09.493 --> 15:11.259
I'm not Derek Jeter.

15:11.293 --> 15:12.494
I like girls.

15:12.528 --> 15:13.661
Ugh, come on, Chris.

15:13.696 --> 15:14.763
Girls are terrible.

15:14.798 --> 15:15.965
They're always backstabbing

15:15.999 --> 15:18.099
and giving each other
phony compliments.

15:18.133 --> 15:21.469
Oh, wow, you are definitely
not afraid of dessert.

15:21.504 --> 15:23.137
You know, I wish I
were secure enough

15:23.172 --> 15:25.473
to throw on any old thing
and call it an outfit.

15:25.508 --> 15:28.409
Come on, you have
so much body confidence.

15:28.444 --> 15:31.111
I mean, who wouldn't
with those strong legs?

15:31.145 --> 15:32.714
So muscular.

15:32.748 --> 15:35.950
I'm jealous of how thick
with strength they are.

15:35.985 --> 15:37.252
Hey, I like your tie.

15:37.286 --> 15:38.285
Thanks.

15:38.320 --> 15:42.223
♪

15:42.258 --> 15:44.192
Come on, Chris,
he'll do all the work.

15:44.225 --> 15:45.626
I said no, Meg.

15:45.660 --> 15:47.060
I'll pay you
a hundred bucks.

15:47.095 --> 15:48.862
Oh, fine, I'll
keep it in my bum.

15:48.897 --> 15:50.430
There'll be
plenty of room.

15:50.465 --> 15:53.133
That's my sarcastic way of
saying it's not gonna happen.

15:53.167 --> 15:54.301
Good day, Meg.

15:54.335 --> 15:56.904
Oh, it's gonna happen.

16:02.110 --> 16:04.077
(doorbell rings)

16:04.112 --> 16:05.545
Oh, hi, Meg.

16:05.579 --> 16:06.746
Hi, Mr. Quagmire.

16:06.780 --> 16:07.964
What can I do for you?

16:07.998 --> 16:10.032
I-I was wondering
if I could borrow some roofies?

16:10.067 --> 16:12.435
Oh, sure, sure,
just a sec.

16:12.469 --> 16:13.836
Roofies, huh?

16:13.870 --> 16:15.705
Pretty big pill for
such a little girl.

16:15.739 --> 16:18.274
Yeah, I know, but I asked
someone to do me a favor,

16:18.308 --> 16:19.909
and they're not too keen
on doing it.

16:19.943 --> 16:21.410
Oh, I know what
they're for, honey.

16:21.445 --> 16:23.011
So, how's school?

16:23.045 --> 16:24.246
Oh, good, thanks.

16:24.280 --> 16:25.647
Studies going well?

16:25.682 --> 16:28.183
Yeah, yeah, mostly A's and B's
so far this semester.

16:28.217 --> 16:29.851
Oh, that's so great.

16:29.885 --> 16:31.870
Seeing anyone
special these days?

16:31.904 --> 16:33.705
Hey, obviously, right?

16:33.739 --> 16:35.490
(laughter)
Of course, yeah.

16:35.524 --> 16:37.226
Okay, well, listen, good
luck with everything.

16:37.260 --> 16:39.094
And, uh, call me
if you get arrested.

16:39.128 --> 16:41.496
I will. Thanks.

16:41.530 --> 16:43.265
That's what
it's all about, Glenn.

16:43.299 --> 16:45.533
Don't rape it back,
rape it forward.

16:50.239 --> 16:51.573
All right,
I talked to Chris,

16:51.606 --> 16:54.108
and he totally wants
to hook up with you, too.

16:54.142 --> 16:55.210
No way! Really?

16:55.244 --> 16:57.045
I didn't even
know he was gay.

16:57.079 --> 16:58.912
It's just that
he's not as comfortable

16:58.948 --> 17:00.681
with his sexuality
as you are yet,

17:00.715 --> 17:03.384
so he's gonna need
to pretend to be asleep

17:03.418 --> 17:04.585
while it's happening.

17:04.619 --> 17:06.320
Oh, he's a snooze-juicer.

17:06.354 --> 17:07.621
Okay.

17:07.656 --> 17:10.423
Wow, I didn't know Chris
had this dark side to him.

17:10.457 --> 17:13.260
Oh, yeah,
Chris has a major dark side.

17:13.295 --> 17:16.763
My dad is actually
really scared of him.

17:17.532 --> 17:20.134
(creaking)
Wha...

17:20.168 --> 17:21.768
Who's there?

17:21.802 --> 17:25.672
Go back to sleep, Dad.

17:25.706 --> 17:27.707
Okay.

17:30.978 --> 17:32.979
(whimpering)

17:35.115 --> 17:38.450
You're very
precious to me.

17:41.821 --> 17:43.622
Chris, I made
some Kool-Aid!

17:43.656 --> 17:44.890
You want some?

17:44.924 --> 17:46.392
Sure!

17:57.337 --> 17:59.086
Chris, what are you doing
in my room?

17:59.122 --> 18:00.722
Nothing.
Yes, you were.

18:00.756 --> 18:02.724
You were putting something
in my drawer.

18:02.757 --> 18:04.825
What's this?

18:04.860 --> 18:06.161
(sighs)
Look, Meg,

18:06.195 --> 18:08.230
I know you've been having
a hard time lately,

18:08.264 --> 18:10.548
so I wanted
to give you something

18:10.582 --> 18:13.451
that means a lot to me.

18:13.485 --> 18:15.519
Oh, I remember this.

18:15.554 --> 18:17.788
This was the trip
our family took to the Cape.

18:17.823 --> 18:19.190
Ugh, it was miserable.

18:19.224 --> 18:21.659
It was raining, and Mom and
Dad fought the whole time.

18:21.693 --> 18:23.094
You taught me how
to hunt squirrels

18:23.128 --> 18:24.095
with poisoned cheese,

18:24.129 --> 18:25.730
and then you took me
to the hospital

18:25.764 --> 18:28.332
when the squirrels tricked me
into eating the cheese.

18:28.366 --> 18:31.651
Chris, you kept this photo
all these years?

18:31.686 --> 18:34.237
Yeah, it's gotten me
through a lot of tough times.

18:34.271 --> 18:36.473
Like when Felicity
cut her hair.

18:36.507 --> 18:38.141
What?!

18:38.176 --> 18:40.710
Aw, thanks, Chris.

18:40.746 --> 18:42.412
That was really
thoughtful of you.

18:42.446 --> 18:45.081
Hey, so can I have
some of that Kool-Aid now?

18:45.116 --> 18:46.448
No.

18:46.484 --> 18:48.485
No, actually you can't.

19:05.069 --> 19:06.769
Oh, Chris, hi.

19:06.803 --> 19:08.370
I didn't realize
you'd be awake.

19:08.405 --> 19:09.638
What?

19:09.672 --> 19:12.073
Well, Meg said you'd be asleep,
but it's fine.

19:12.108 --> 19:13.242
I can work with this.

19:13.276 --> 19:14.810
Oh, hell no!

19:14.844 --> 19:15.978
Meg!

19:16.012 --> 19:18.046
Oh, my God.

19:18.081 --> 19:20.314
Kent, I just texted you
that the plan was off.

19:20.349 --> 19:23.218
Meg, what the hell
were you planning on doing?!

19:23.253 --> 19:24.987
Oh, Chris,
I'm so sorry.

19:25.021 --> 19:26.654
I was so obsessed
with Kent

19:26.688 --> 19:28.423
that I-I guess I wasn't
thinking straight.

19:28.457 --> 19:31.559
I'm just glad I stopped before
I did a really terrible thing.

19:31.593 --> 19:33.961
Terrible thing?
What terrible thing?

19:33.996 --> 19:37.298
Well, like I said,
I-I changed my mind.

19:37.332 --> 19:38.599
I-I didn't do it.

19:38.634 --> 19:39.867
But, um...

19:39.902 --> 19:41.102
I was...

19:41.136 --> 19:43.037
kind of gonna...

19:43.071 --> 19:44.222
roofie you.

19:44.256 --> 19:46.307
What?!
What is wrong with you?!

19:46.341 --> 19:48.760
And, Kent, I owe you
an apology, too.

19:48.794 --> 19:51.411
I lied when I told you that
Chris wanted to sleep with you.

19:51.446 --> 19:52.547
Save it, Meg!

19:52.581 --> 19:53.880
I don't need your apologies!

19:53.915 --> 19:56.416
I can see now
that you're a complete psycho!

19:59.554 --> 20:02.339
Boy, clothes sure are a prison,
aren't they?

20:04.609 --> 20:06.843
Lot of drumroll for nothing.

20:06.878 --> 20:08.111
What's this?

20:08.146 --> 20:10.146
Ooh, candy!

20:21.208 --> 20:22.291
Hey, Meg.

20:22.325 --> 20:23.592
I heard what happened.

20:23.627 --> 20:25.644
Yeah, Kent hates me now.

20:25.678 --> 20:27.112
You made a mistake.

20:27.147 --> 20:28.447
I know you feel terrible,

20:28.482 --> 20:30.048
but you're not
a bad person, Meg.

20:30.082 --> 20:31.750
You just need
to get back out there,

20:31.785 --> 20:33.852
and someday,
maybe you'll find the right guy.

20:33.886 --> 20:35.521
You really
think so, Brian?

20:35.555 --> 20:36.921
I know so.

20:36.956 --> 20:39.090
All it takes is one guy
making one mistake,

20:39.124 --> 20:40.559
one drunken night.

20:40.594 --> 20:41.727
Sperm finding a fertile egg.

20:42.433 --> 20:44.200
You refusing to do
what a sane woman would do.

20:44.735 --> 20:46.369
You got him, Meg.
You got him for life.

20:47.348 --> 20:48.598
Thanks, Brian.
No problem.

20:49.700 --> 20:51.945
Hey, do either of you know
what poison ivy looks like?

20:51.946 --> 21:52.946
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru